OL,3,AKellogg's admits snap, crackle and pop
OL,4,Ais quieter after uproar over Rice
OL,5,AKrispies recipe change
OL,6,
OL,7,FA Kellogg's spokesperson said retaining
OL,8,Fthe iconic sound had been a "huge
OL,9,Ffocus" when designing the new recipe,
OL,10,Fbut that customers "might notice that
OL,11,Fthe sound may be quieter and not as
OL,12,Finstant as before".
OL,14,FThe firm was responding to complaints
OL,15,Fonline that the taste of the breakfast
OL,16,Fstaples had changed, with some fans
OL,17,Fadding they missed the "pop" sound.
